{#- The Menu shell (docs/features/navigation README §4.12 "Phone panel", MENU-02b; §4.3 overlay, NAV-13; decision 87): an
    empty <dialog id="menu-layer"> at the end of <body> (block nav_layers, web only - bar-free and auth pages empty it).
    The phone panel and the desktop overlay move the page's one #site-menu in here when they open and back to its slot
    when they close (assets/controllers/menu_layer_controller.js) - never a second copy of the Menu. The panel opens
    with show(), never showModal() (the bottom bar stays usable); the desktop overlay (768-1279 px, and a link to `menu`
    in the rail state) with showModal() as .menu-layer--overlay: a sheet from the left, this header as its own 64 px
    one (× · logo; "Menu" names the dialog), the Menu as in the docked column - the search field is the panel's only.
    The header is logo · Menu · ×: on phones × sits where the ☰ that opened it is (the top bar's right end, owner
    2026-10-16); the overlay, opened by the ☰ at the top bar's left, draws × first (CSS order, _nav-layout.scss).
    Closed it is display: none.
    data-menu-paths: the `menu` page in every locale - a link to any of them opens the panel on phones
    (assets/navigation/menu_links.js). data-menu-layer-place-value: the page's place (a tap on its tab only closes).
    Shared-cacheable for guests: nothing in here depends on the visitor but the logo's target (Home: hub / homepage).
    The `menu` page renders the Menu as its content (nav_menu_slot_off): no shell there.
    Chrome markup rules (implementation plan §3.2): no heading element, no form; data-nav on every link and button.
    The search field at the top of the body (MENU-03) is the page search's second instance. -#}
{%- if not (nav_menu_slot_off ?? false) -%}
{%- set menu_paths = ['cs', 'en', 'de', 'es', 'fr', 'ja']|map(locale => path('menu', {_locale: locale})) -%}
<dialog id="menu-layer" class="menu-layer" aria-labelledby="menu-layer-title" data-controller="menu-layer"
    data-menu-paths={{ menu_paths|json_attribute }}
    data-menu-layer-place-value="{{ nav_location().place.value }}">
    <div class="menu-layer-header">
        {#- -#}<a class="menu-layer-logo" href="{{ logged_user.profile is not null ? path('hub') : path('homepage') }}" data-nav="menu/none/logo"><img width="36" height="32" src="{{ asset('img/speedpuzzling-logo.svg') }}" alt="MySpeedPuzzling"></a>
        {#- -#}<span class="menu-layer-title" id="menu-layer-title">{{ 'nav.menu.title'|trans }}</span>
        {#- -#}<button type="button" class="menu-layer-close" data-menu-layer-target="close" data-action="menu-layer#close" data-nav="menu/none/close" aria-label="{{ 'nav.menu.close'|trans }}"><i class="bi bi-x-lg" aria-hidden="true"></i></button>
    </div>
    <div class="menu-layer-body" data-menu-layer-target="body">
        {#- The Menu's search field (MENU-03, R3): the second GlobalSearch, sticky under the header - the first in the DOM is
            the page's (decision 87). Typed in here, its results ("Pages & settings" first, then puzzlers and puzzles)
            show here: the shell gets .is-searching and #site-menu, moved in after it when the panel opens, steps aside -
            same layer, same history entry. -#}
        <div class="menu-layer-search" data-menu-layer-search><twig:GlobalSearch key="menu" surface="menu" :limit="8" /></div>
    </div>
</dialog>
{%- endif -%}
